# `npm run format` is `prettier --write .` over the whole repo. Everything below
# is either byte-exact test data or generated output, where a reformat is a
# silent breakage rather than a cleanup.

# Committed projection snapshots (Task 2.6). `toMatchFileSnapshot` compares raw
# file content untrimmed, and Prettier's JSON printer collapses a one-element
# array — `"tags": [\n  "degraded"\n]` becomes `"tags": ["degraded"]` — so a
# single `npm run format` would red the entire golden suite until every snapshot
# was regenerated. Asserted by golden-replay.test.ts.
src/**/__snapshots__/

# Captured fixture sets. `.jsonl` has no Prettier parser and is skipped anyway,
# but these directories also carry `.json` sidecars (Task 1.7 commits a
# `manifest.json` per set) that live under the SCRUBBING.md sign-off — a format
# run must not rewrite data a human signed off on byte-for-byte.
fixtures/

# Generated / vendored, mirroring eslint.config.js's ignore list.
dist/
coverage/
ui/dist/
package-lock.json
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Release automation (Task 8.5): release-please writes CHANGELOG.md and rewrites
# its manifest on every release PR; reformatting either would fight the bot.
CHANGELOG.md
.release-please-manifest.json
release-please-config.json
